                    },
                    "message": "Would this be better as its own type?  And then the Labels array could use it.\nOr do you prefer it how it is?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/legacy.json",
                    "line": 913,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "I wonder if there is any underlying difference that can be used or what the restriction is on ```Label```. \n\nI did not give too much thought about it since it looks like an optional property.\n\nIf there is no restriction it makes no difference from a schema perspective,\nif we define a new type or not. Then it might as well be ```string```."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/legacy.json",
                    "line": 913,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm sure it all boils down to a string.  I guess at this point I'll call it good enough so we can get these in, unless you'd like to change it."
                }
